      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(macos): preserve OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH/STATE_DIR/PROFILE in launch-at-login plist (fixes #98594) (AI-assisted)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen a user launches the macOS OpenClaw app with a custom profile (e.g. `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=/tmp/oc-state`), then enables \"Launch at login\", the generated LaunchAgent plist only preserves `PATH` in `EnvironmentVariables`. On next login, the app starts without `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH` or `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR` and falls back to the default `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` profile — silently losing the user's custom configuration.\n\nThis is inconsistent with the Node launchd installer, which correctly passes `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR`, `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH`, and other profile variables through the env-wrapper mechanism.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`LaunchAgentManager.plistContents(bundlePath:)` hardcoded only `PATH` in the `EnvironmentVariables` dict. The fix adds a `profileEnvironmentEntries()` helper that reads `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH`, `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR`, and `OPENCLAW_PROFILE` from the current process environment and includes non-empty values in the generated plist.\n\nThe `environment` parameter defaults to `ProcessInfo.processInfo.environment` in production but accepts an explicit dictionary for testability.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers who run OpenClaw with a custom `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR` or `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH` and enable \"Launch at login\" will now have their profile correctly preserved across login sessions. No more silent fallback to the default profile.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Behavior addressed:** macOS launch-at-login LaunchAgent plist now includes `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH`, `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR`, and `OPENCLAW_PROFILE` from the process environment.\n- **Environment tested:** macOS arm64, Swift 6.1, SPM test suite.\n- **Steps run after the patch:** `cd apps/macos && swift test --filter GatewayLaunchAgentManagerTests`\n- **Evidence after fix:**\n```\n◇ Suite GatewayLaunchAgentManagerTests started.\n✔ Test \"plist contents preserves profile environment variables\" passed after 0.004 seconds.\n✔ Test \"plist contents omits empty profile environment variables\" passed after 0.004 seconds.\n✔ Test \"attach only runtime override does not uninstall gateway launch agent\" passed after 0.002 seconds.\n✔ Test \"launch agent plist snapshot parses args and env\" passed after 0.002 seconds.\n✔ Test \"launch agent plist snapshot allows missing bind\" passed after 0.002 seconds.\n✔ Suite GatewayLaunchAgentManagerTests passed after 0.004 seconds.\n✔ Test run with 5 tests in 1 suite passed after 0.004 seconds.\n```\n- **Observed result after fix:** The `plistContents()` function correctly includes `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH`, `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR`, and `OPENCLAW_PROFILE` in the generated plist's `EnvironmentVariables` when provided, and omits them when empty.\n- **What was not tested:** Live launch-at-login cycle with actual macOS login/logout. The fix is validated through unit tests that verify the plist generation output.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior addressed:** macOS launch-at-login LaunchAgent plist now includes `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH`, `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR`, and `OPENCLAW_PROFILE` from the process environment.\n- **Environment tested:** macOS arm64, Swift 6.1, SPM test suite.\n- **Steps run after the patch:** `cd apps/macos && swift test --filter GatewayLaunchAgentManagerTests`\n- **Evidence after fix:**\n```\n◇ Suite GatewayLaunchAgentManagerTests started.\n✔ Test \"plist contents preserves profile environment variables\" passed after 0.004 seconds.\n✔ Test \"plist contents omits empty profile environment variables\" passed after 0.004 seconds.\n✔ Test \"attach only runtime override does not uninstall gateway launch agent\" passed after 0.002 seconds.\n✔ Test \"launch agent plist snapshot parses args and env\" passed after 0.002 seconds.\n✔ Test \"launch agent plist snapshot allows missing bind\" passed after 0.002 seconds.\n✔ Suite GatewayLaunchAgentManagerTests passed after 0.004 seconds.\n✔ Test run with 5 tests in 1 suite passed after 0.004 seconds.\n```\n- **Observed result after fix:** The `plistContents()` function correctly includes `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH`, `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR`, and `OPENCLAW_PROFILE` in the generated plist's `EnvironmentVariables` when provided, and omits them when empty.\n- **What was not tested:** Live launch-at-login cycle with actual macOS login/logout. The fix is validated through unit tests that verify the plist generation output.\n\n- [x] AI-assisted (Hermes Agent)\n",
        "branch": "fix/macos-launch-at-login-profile-env",
